WEBVTT

00:28:28.504 --> 00:28:30.827
I'm trying to see
the intent of the individual,

00:28:30.851 --> 00:28:32.075
first and foremost.

00:28:33.269 --> 00:28:35.581
AG: Think about the interviews
in your workplace,

00:28:35.605 --> 00:28:38.100
and where you might be able
to add some work samples.

00:28:38.124 --> 00:28:40.988
If you're hiring people to write
an owner's manual for a car,

00:28:41.012 --> 00:28:42.569
or a user manual for a computer,

00:28:42.593 --> 00:28:45.363
you could ask candidates
to write one during the interview.

00:28:45.387 --> 00:28:47.982
If you're evaluating people
for customer service roles,

00:28:48.006 --> 00:28:50.410
you can have them meet
with some unhappy customers,

00:28:50.434 --> 00:28:52.265
or play one yourself.

00:28:53.367 --> 00:28:54.543
Research suggests

00:28:54.567 --> 00:28:57.059
that work samples can get around
some of the problems

00:28:57.083 --> 00:28:58.662
with traditional job interviews.

00:28:58.686 --> 00:29:01.764
Instead of asking questions
and listening to what candidates say,